<title>TANZANIA: Tanzania raises fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Tanzania raises fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DAR ES SALAAM 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petrol and diesel fuel prices in Tanzania were increased by up to 4.35 percent on Sunday, reflecting higher world oil prices, the Tanzanian Patroleum Development Corporation announced.</p>
<p>Premium petrol now costs 360 shillings ($0.58) a litre, up from 345 shillings, while diesel fuel costs 285 shillings ($0.46), up from 276 shillings.</p>
<p>Fuel prices have remained unchanged since last January.</p>
<p>($1=620 Tanzanian shillings)</p>
</text>
